Found under k315 (ocp-choices-worker, 2026-10-31). The same bug as k315's robocop: no, at other switches: a non-empty string is true in Perl, so a YAML 1.1 word (no, off, n, "false", False) reads as ON.
- gpu.enabled (`gpu: { enabled: no }` turns the GPU stack on)
- gpu.toolkit
- gpu.amd.labeller, gpu.amd.metrics, gpu.amd.integrated
- lbipam
- nocert
- system.ntp

Shape of the fix (k315 precedent): refuse anything but a YAML boolean or 1/0 in validate(), with the "; write KEY: false" hint for a string that spells a boolean (Config::_is_switch / _boolean_hint), and make each accessor refuse the same way (one helper per switch, so validate() and the accessor cannot disagree). Check every reader of each switch, as k315 did for robocop_enabled. gpu.amd.integrated: coordinate with k253 (the same key, cluster-wide) -- do this after k253 lands or include it there.

Done = each switch refuses a string in validate() with a hint, the accessors agree (t/296-style sweep), the three real configs (cihq, citiai, amdlab) still give 0 errors.

